{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Moses grew.</b> But has it not already been written, ״וַיִּגְדַּל הַיֶּלֶד״? Rabbi Yehudah son of Rabbi Ilai said: the first is for stature, and the second for greatness — Pharaoh appointed him over his household." "<b>And he saw their suffering.</b> He set his eyes and his heart to be grieved over them." "<b>An Egyptian man.</b> He was a taskmaster appointed over the officers of Israel, and would station them at unfortified towns for their labor." "<b>striking a Hebrew man.</b> Striking him and subjugating him. And he was the husband of Shelomit daughter of Dibri, and he had set his eyes on her. At night he stationed him and took him out of his house, and he returned and entered the house and lay with his wife — she thinking he was her husband. The man returned to his home and became aware of the matter, and when that Egyptian saw that he had become aware of the matter, he would strike him and subjugate him all day."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:16.517094431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}